{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["And the fourth generation shall come back here — the one who explains this as the fourth generation of Israel is mistaken, for once He set a fixed term of four hundred years, what difference does it make whether it is the fourth generation or the fifth? In any case they would delay four hundred years. Rather, the Holy One, blessed be He, gave a reason for His words: why do I need to delay four hundred years — after the fourth generation of the Amorites, Israel shall return here, a generation being one hundred years, as found in tractate Eduyot. And so four generations — for even though the inhabitants of the land have sinned and their judgment is for the land to vomit out its inhabitants, I must wait four generations, as written: פוקד עוון אבות על בנים ועל שלשים ועל ריבעים לשונאי — perhaps the sons will return in repentance, for the time of reckoning that I am destined to exact from the sinning Amorites has not yet been completed until here, until after the fourth generation of the Amorites, as written: על שלשים וגו׳. This is its plain sense."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The bracketed phrase [טועה הוא] appears in the source; rendered as 'is mistaken' integrated into the sentence."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:23.935441005Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}